# Media & cards — full spec

Media apps (RuForge, anything with posters/thumbnails/album art) live and die on card treatment. This is the detailed version of `design-style` §9.

## Card type → aspect ratio → meaning

| Context | Aspect | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Hero / featured | full-bleed 16:9 or 21:9 cinematic | the title's atmosphere fills the screen |
| Top-10 / poster grid / "browse" | **2:3 portrait poster** | poster art is the content; art = the card |
| Continue-watching / in-progress | **16:9 landscape thumbnail** | it's a resume frame/scene, wider, not a poster |
| Album / square art | **1:1 square** | matches the source art; never force to another ratio |

The ratio itself tells the user what kind of thing they're looking at. A portrait card and a landscape card in the same view = two different content types. Use that.

## Image rules (hard)
- `object-fit: cover` always. Crop overflow. Never letterbox/pad onto a solid color.
- The frame's aspect ratio matches the intended display ratio so cover-crop looks intentional.
- Round corners with `--r-media` (16–20px).
- Optional bottom scrim (`linear-gradient(transparent, rgba(0,0,0,0.7))`) when text sits over the art, for legibility.
- Hover: subtle `transform: scale(1.03)` + optional brightness lift. Fast (`--dur-fast`), eased. No glow.

## Positional info (learned conventions — don't reinvent)
- **Resume/duration timestamp:** bottom-right of the thumbnail, small pill or plain text on a tiny scrim. Every user knows to look bottom-right.
- **Rank badge** (TOP 01): top-left corner, small accent-colored tag.
- **Progress bar** (partially watched): thin bar pinned to the very bottom edge of the thumbnail, accent fill.
- **Metadata line** (rating · year · type): UNDER the card, dot-separated, `--text-muted`. The rating star/number can carry the accent.

## Section structure
- Header: short title, optionally a **left accent bar** (small vertical tick in the accent color, Cineby `| Continue watching` style).
- Horizontal scroll row of cards with consistent gap (`--space-4`).
- **Scroll affordance:** left/right arrow on a soft radial shadow that fades into the app background (same hue, darkened). Reads as atmosphere pointing the way, NOT a solid button chip. Appears on hover of the row.
- **Section differentiation:** if two rows carry different value, vary card size or art treatment. Don't clone the same row three times with different titles.

## Nav / chrome blur
- **Nav bar:** solid (or transparent-over-hero-media, then solid once scrolled). NOT frosted glass.
- **Search bar, floating overlays, command palettes:** glassy — `backdrop-filter: blur(...)` + translucent fill. This is where glass belongs.
- Decide blur by element role. Never blanket-glass the whole UI.

## Texture
- **Grain:** subtle noise on large flat surfaces to kill gradient banding (very low opacity overlay).
- **Hero gradient/mesh:** a soft gradient or mesh behind hero content; long bottom scrim so content fades up out of the art (Cineby hero pattern).
- Keep both subtle — texture is seasoning, not the meal.
